{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"The acceptance criteria are reworded so the completion verifier can check each one. The S6 close showed that it rejects runtime-only evidence unless the criterion is tagged `[non-codebase]` with provenance.\n- The old criterion 1 is split in 2. The loader grep stays a codebase check. `python -m rebar.reconciler --help` becomes a `[non-codebase]` criterion.\n- The old criterion 4 is split in 2. The deletions stay a codebase grep. The ratchet `new=0` result becomes a `[non-codebase]` criterion.\n- The release-notes criterion is now checked by reading `CHANGELOG.md` and `docs/release-notes.md`.\n- The criterion numbers in Child decomposition are renumbered to match.\n\nEvidence for `python -m rebar.reconciler --help`, run 2026-10-22 at origin/main ad630728043:\n- command: `env -i HOME=$HOME PATH=/usr/bin:/bin .venv/bin/python -I -m rebar.reconciler --help`, from `.rebar/scratch/lane-ebf5/bare_help/`, outside the package tree;\n- exit 0, and the output begins `usage: rebar.reconciler [-h] [--repo-root REPO_ROOT] [--mode MODE] ...`;\n- `rebar.reconciler.__spec__.loader` is the standard `SourceFileLoader`, with no by-path loader.\n\nThe ratchet evidence will be recorded at the S7 merge."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792657386098212410,"uuid":"c60aca3a-0f86-4d3e-a114-a5b283cd84d1"}